sequenceDiagram
    participant Server as Polar git server
    participant Cassini
    participant Observer as Scheduler observer
    participant Processor as Scheduler processor
    participant Graph as Neo4j
    participant Target as Target agent
    participant CA as ConfigurationActor (in the target)

    Server-)Cassini: RepoChanged
    Cassini-)Observer: RepoChanged (for its repository)
    Observer->>Server: git pull --ff-only (mTLS, workload certificate)
    Observer->>Observer: evaluate changed item, refuse any file with an import or without exactly payload and signature
    opt early check, same rules as the target's
        Observer->>Observer: verify signature, signer, version, drop and log an invalid item
    end
    Observer-)Cassini: GitScheduleChange {whole document}
    Cassini-)Processor: GitScheduleChange
    Processor->>Graph: upsert the schedule node (document stored as received)
    Processor-)Cassini: ScheduleNotification {whole document} on agent.<id>.schedule
    Cassini-)Target: ScheduleNotification
    Target->>CA: apply(document)

    Note over CA: the receiver never trusts the relay: it verifies for itself, in order
    CA->>CA: 1. exactly payload and signature, no import
    CA->>CA: 2. chain to the pinned Polar CA, certificate valid, digitalSignature, P-256
    CA->>CA: 3. signature over canonical JSON of payload
    CA->>CA: 4. signer holds c:update-policy (Cedar later)
    CA->>CA: 5. signer not revoked (a hook only, for now)
    CA->>CA: 6. version above the last applied
    alt every check passes
        CA->>CA: apply_overrides: Dynamic only, values parse, section relations hold
        CA-)Target: ConfigChanged {version, names}
        Target->>CA: current() and use the new values
        CA->>CA: record the update (names, never values)
    else any check fails
        CA->>CA: refuse whole, old values stay, record the reason and version
        Note over CA: telling the author is not designed yet
    end
